INT. SCHOOL HALLWAY - DAY

A display case sits against the wall. Inside, a tiny, glittering stamp shines. The Golden Beetle Stamp. It is the color of deep purple #5B4B8A and gold.

REYANSH (10) stands in front of the glass. He is a South Asian boy. His hair is swept to one side. He wears a navy tracksuit top with white piping. A purple hearing aid, color #5B4B8A, sits behind his left ear. Reyansh is a deaf boy who has profound bilateral hearing loss. He looks at the stamp with intense focus.

Reyansh pulls a folded paper fortune-teller from his pocket. It is made of pale lavender paper, color #F0EFF4. He slides his fingers inside. He snaps it open and closed. East, West, North, South. He wants that stamp.

ROHAN (10), a non-disabled classmate, runs up and taps Reyansh on the shoulder. Rohan speaks, his lips moving quickly. Captions appear on screen for all spoken dialogue.

ROHAN
(via captions)
Come on, Reyansh! The assembly is starting! The famous bug guy is here!

Reyansh nods. He tucks his paper fortune-teller back into his pocket.

INT. ASSEMBLY HALL - DAY

Hundreds of students sit on the floor. The room is filled with a low rumble of chatter.

At the front, a large banner reads: WELCOME DR. RONALD, CHIEF ENTOMOLOGIST.

Mrs. Gable, the principal, stands at a microphone. She is a non-disabled woman. Her mouth moves in wide, enthusiastic shapes.

Reyansh sits in the third row. A speech-to-text app on his tablet screen translates her words in real-time.

MRS. GABLE
(via tablet text)
And he has brought the rare Golden Beetle Stamp to show us today!

On the stage, DR. RONALD (40s) steps up. He wears a tweed jacket. He has a wide, toothy grin. He waves.

The non-disabled students around Reyansh clap and cheer.

Reyansh does not watch the slides of beetles. He watches Dr. Ronald's face.

Dr. Ronald smiles, but the muscles around his eyes do not move. His left cheek twitches twice. It is a microexpression of extreme nerves.

Reyansh taps his chin. He pulls out his paper fortune-teller. He flips it open. Inside, a drawn eye stares back at him.

Dr. Ronald reaches for the glass box on the presentation table. His hand shakes. He grips the box too tightly.

Behind Dr. Ronald stands his ASSISTANT (30s). The assistant is a non-disabled man in a gray suit.

The assistant looks at the crowd. He raises his hands and starts making strange, wavy gestures.

Rohan leans over to Reyansh. He points at the assistant. Rohan mimics the gestures, laughing.

ROHAN
(via captions)
Look, he is signing to you! Is that sign language?

Reyansh looks at the assistant's hands. The movements are clumsy, empty, and mean nothing. It is fake sign language.

Reyansh signs back to Rohan with quick, precise hands. Captions translate his signs on screen.

REYANSH
(signing)
That is not signing. That is a secret code.

Reyansh watches the assistant's fingers. The assistant taps his left shoulder, then points to the side door, then holds up three fingers.

Reyansh looks at his tablet screen. The speech-to-text app displays Dr. Ronald's voice.

DR. RONALD
(via tablet text)
And now, I will demonstrate how we preserve these precious specimens.

Dr. Ronald reaches into his pocket. He pulls out a small, purple velvet box.

Reyansh watches Dr. Ronald's mouth. The doctor's lips tighten into a thin line. He holds his breath. His eyes dart toward the side door where a black duffel bag sits.

Reyansh realizes the plan. The assistant's fake signs were instructions. The doctor is going to swap the real stamp with a fake one during the demonstration.

Reyansh stands up. He taps Rohan and signs quickly.

REYANSH
(signing)
He is going to steal it.

Rohan looks confused.

ROHAN
(via captions)
What? He is a famous doctor!

Reyansh does not wait. He walks down the center aisle toward the stage.

Mrs. Gable notices him. She frowns and waves her hands, gesturing for him to sit down.

Reyansh reaches the front of the stage. He taps his tablet. He types a message quickly. He turns the screen toward Mrs. Gable and Dr. Ronald.

REYANSH
(via tablet text)
That man is not Dr. Ronald. He is an impostor.

The room goes quiet.

Dr. Ronald laughs. His voice booms through the speakers. He looks at Mrs. Gable.

DR. RONALD
(via captions)
Ah, the young man must be confused. It is hard for some to follow along.

Mrs. Gable steps forward. She looks at Reyansh with pity.

MRS. GABLE
(via captions)
Reyansh, dear, please go back to your seat. Dr. Ronald is our guest.

Reyansh stands firm. He is a deaf boy, and he knows what he saw. He points at Dr. Ronald's left sleeve.

Reyansh signs with sharp, clear movements.

REYANSH
(signing)
His face lied when he said his name. His hands shook because he is nervous. And his assistant just signaled him to make the switch. Look in his sleeve!

The assistant panics. He runs toward the side door.

Rohan, watching from the third row, sticks his foot out. The assistant trips and falls flat on the floor. A second purple velvet box slides out of his pocket and rolls across the floor.

Mrs. Gable gasps. She picks up the fallen box and opens it. Inside is a cheap, plastic replica of the Golden Beetle Stamp.

Dr. Ronald steps back. His face loses all color. He clutches his left sleeve.

Mrs. Gable walks over to Dr. Ronald. She pulls back his sleeve. The real Golden Beetle Stamp, glowing in its deep purple #5B4B8A and gold case, is tucked inside his cuff.

The crowd of students erupts into cheers.

Mrs. Gable turns to Dr. Ronald and his assistant.

MRS. GABLE
(via captions)
I think you both need to leave. Now.

Two security guards lead the impostors away.

Mrs. Gable turns to Reyansh. She holds the real Golden Beetle Stamp. Her face is full of awe.

MRS. GABLE
(via captions)
You saw what none of us could hear.

She hands the Golden Beetle Stamp to Reyansh.

MRE. GABLE
(via captions)
This belongs to you. The ultimate puzzle solver.

Reyansh takes the stamp. It fits perfectly in his palm. He smiles.

He pulls his paper fortune-teller from his pocket. He slips the stamp safely inside the center fold.

He is still the same deaf boy, with his navy tracksuit and his purple hearing aid. He did not need to hear a single word to catch the thief.

Reyansh signs to Rohan.

REYANSH
(signing)
Let us go back to class.

They walk out of the hall together.